<BaseLayout title="Stay-at-Home Parent Calculator: Work vs Childcare Costs | DollarAngle" description="Free stay-at-home parent calculator comparing take-home pay against daycare, commuting and other costs. See monthly cash impact and lost retirement match.">
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
<div class="container tool-page"><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › <a href="/tools">Money Tools</a> › Stay-at-Home Parent Calculator</nav>
<header class="intro"><p class="kicker">FREE FAMILY FINANCE CALCULATOR</p><h1>Should One Parent Stay Home? <span>Compare the Real Childcare Costs</span></h1><p>Childcare and work-related spending can change the picture of an annual salary. Explore a financial comparison without treating a family's decision as purely mathematical.</p></header>
<StayHomeParentCalculator />
<article class="guide"><h2>How much does working really add after childcare?</h2><p>Begin with the salary of the parent considering a career break. Estimate income and payroll deductions, divide the resulting take-home pay by 12, and subtract monthly daycare plus work-related costs such as commuting, clothing or meals.</p>
<h2>Worked example</h2><p>If a parent earns $60,000 gross annually and assumes 22% deductions, estimated monthly take-home is $3,900. Subtract $1,400 in childcare and $350 in work-related costs to get <strong>$2,150 in monthly cash contribution</strong>. If the employer also contributes $2,400 annually in retirement matching, leaving the job may additionally forgo $200 monthly in retirement contributions. That match is shown separately, not counted as spendable cash.</p>
<h2>Financial considerations beyond today's paycheck</h2><p>Think about health coverage, paid leave, promotions, future salary growth, retirement, returning to employment, and the care preferences of your household. An effective tax and payroll deduction rate is a planning assumption, not a substitute for a tax calculation. This tool does not determine the total household tax liability when one spouse changes employment.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>{faqs.map(([q,a])=><details><summary>{q}</summary><p>{a}</p></details>)}
<h2>Related resources</h2><p><a href="/tools/mine-yours-ours-budget-calculator">Set up your shared household budget →</a> <a href="/tools/rent-split-calculator">Explore fair household bill splitting →</a></p><p class="note">Educational estimate, not individualized tax, retirement, employment or financial advice. Enter all amounts in the same currency. Actual childcare and tax treatment depend on your location and circumstances.</p>
</article></div></BaseLayout>
